Subject: [PATCH] Return the invalid SHaRC index when allocation fails

Applies to SHaRC 1.6.5 at 0b9f58bbc8c41736042d4da964830a247e424a00.
A failed insertion must not access unrelated slot zero or stop propagation
to earlier valid vertices. Existing invalid-index guards handle the sentinel.

This software contains source code provided by NVIDIA Corporation.
SHaRC remains subject to its upstream NVIDIA RTX SDKs license; see README.md.

diff --git a/include/HashGridCommon.h b/include/HashGridCommon.h
index bb82326..cdcabe3 100644
--- a/include/HashGridCommon.h
+++ b/include/HashGridCommon.h
@@ -240,7 +240,10 @@ HashGridIndex HashMapInsertEntry(in HashMapData hashMapData, float3 samplePositi
     const HashGridKey hashKey   = HashGridComputeSpatialHash(samplePosition, sampleNormal, gridParameters);
     bool successful             = HashMapInsert(hashMapData, hashKey, cacheIndex);
 
-    return cacheIndex;
+    // An exhausted probe window must not alias an unrelated entry at slot zero.
+    // Existing invalid-index guards skip that entry while preserving propagation
+    // to earlier valid vertices in the update path.
+    return successful ? cacheIndex : HASH_GRID_INVALID_CACHE_INDEX;
 }
 
 HashGridIndex HashMapFindEntry(in HashMapData hashMapData, float3 samplePosition, float3 sampleNormal, HashGridParameters gridParameters)
